Package: searchnet
Title: Network-Embedded Search Simulation Engine
Version: 0.9.2
Authors@R: person("Stephen", "Downing", email = "sdowning@missouri.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R6-based simulation engine for strategic search and adaptation
    on NK fitness landscapes embedded in social networks. Uses RSiena's
    Stochastic Actor-Oriented Model methodology to represent firm activity
    systems as bipartite actor-component networks with endogenous feedback
    loops, coupled degree distributions (K4), and shock/intervention analysis
    via difference-in-differences. Theorem 5 (Brock & Durlauf 2001 recovery)
    establishes that the canonical economic discrete-choice-with-social-
    interactions model is contained as a degenerate special case in the
    many-actor mean-field limit, complementing Theorem 1 (NK reduction in the
    single-actor greedy limit). Formerly known as SaoMNK.
